 bits","assumptions":["Rust integer arithmetic uses checked overflow behavior (debug/test profile); release wrapping arithmetic is outside this draft contract","String case conversion depends on the source and host Unicode tables","Concrete admitted constants require bounded checked evaluation with original parser source links; const fn runtime eligibility alone proves no all-input compile-time behavior","Immutable strings encode scalar values; monomorphic tagged values encode Option/Result; vectors/slices are immutable arrays"],"observation":"checked value results, local scalar mutation, immutable constructors, lazy future polling and named host effects; carried items supply no executable behavior"},"counts":{"executable":0,"executableFunctions":0,"executableConstants":0,"executableTypes":0,"executableConstructors":0,"carried":11,"preserved":12},"items":[{"term":"trivia","name":null,"span":{"start":0,"end":806,"unit":"utf16","byteStart":0,"byteEnd":806},"sha256":"f8d6b095653850e071b9e3f7d3264416e706936b3acc9e18ef25dd67257c0a3e","source":"//! Real macOS Keychain lookups (issue #674).\n//!\n//! These tests read the login Keychain, so they run only when\n//! `ROUTER_TEST_KEYCHAIN=1` is set on macOS: the `macOS Keychain` workflow\n//! creates a throwaway keychain, makes it the default, and seeds it with fake\n//! Claude Code items before running them. Everywhere else they return early,\n//! so no test ever reads a developer's real credential.\n//!\n//! The workflow seeds:\n//!\n//! - `Claude Code-credentials` holding [`SEEDED_ACCESS_TOKEN`] (expiring far in\n//!   the future), the entry Claude Code writes for the default config dir;\n//! - the entry Claude Code writes when `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR` is [`SCOPED_DIR`];\n//! - `~/.claude/.credentials.json` holding [`STALE_FILE_TOKEN`] with an older\n//!   expiry, the stale snapshot issue #249 was about.\n\n","status":"preserved","diagnostic":null,"comment":true},{"term":"mod","name":"common","span":{"start":806,"end":817,"unit"